{"id":"a11d41b3e59a516144c766f9eecb119c00692e8a","axis":"silent","repo":"quarkusio/quarkus","sha":"a11d41b3e59a516144c766f9eecb119c00692e8a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication.adoc","lines":["@@ -1336,6 +1336,10 @@ You can define a link:https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9449.html#name-resource-"," If the DPoP proof nonce is missing or invalid, Quarkus responds with the `401 Unauthorized` status and attaches the expected nonce as the `DPoP-Nonce` header value."," The provider can also use the verified DPoP proof link:https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9449#section-4.2[`jti`] identifier to detect and reject replayed DPoP proofs."," ","+Use the `quarkus.oidc.dpop.proof-age` property to reject DPoP proofs older than the configured duration (default is 2 minutes), calculated from the proof's `iat` (issued at) claim.","+This ensures proofs with timestamps in the past or future are properly rejected. The `quarkus.oidc.token.lifespan-grace` property can optionally add a grace period to tolerate slight clock skews.","+The optional `exp` (expiry) claim is also verified when present.","+"," === Mutual TLS token binding"," "," https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8705[RFC8705] describes a mechanism for binding access tokens to Mutual TLS (mTLS) client authentication certificates."],"additions":4,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/security-oidc-expanded-configuration.adoc","lines":["@@ -952,6 +952,8 @@ Sometimes the roles are contained in the UserInfo response - do `quarkus.oidc.ro"," "," Token bindings are tools for sender-constraining access tokens."," ","+==== Mutual TLS (mTLS)","+"," .MTLS token binding"," [options=\"header\"]"," |====","@@ -964,7 +966,26 @@ Token bindings are tools for sender-constraining access tokens."," "," Please see the xref:security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication.adoc#mutual-tls-token-binding[Mutual TLS token binding] section for more information."," ","-See also the <<bearer-token-source-properties>> section for details about enabling a Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP) binding.","+[[dpop-token-binding]]","+==== Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP)","+","+https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc9449[RFC 9449] describes a Demonstrating Proof of Possession (DPoP) mechanism for cryptographically binding an access token to the client.","+To enable the DPoP binding, set `quarkus.oidc.token.authorization-scheme=DPoP` to accept the DPoP access tokens sent as `Authorization: DPoP <token>`.","+See the <<bearer-token-source-properties>> section for more information.","+","+Use the following properties to configure the DPoP binding restrictions:","+","+.DPoP token binding","+[options=\"header\"]","+|====","+|Property | Default |Description","+","+|quarkus.oidc.dpop.proof-age | 2 minutes | Maximum acceptable age of DPoP proof","+|====","+","+The `quarkus.oidc.dpop.proof-age` property can be used to configure the DPoP proof freshness validation.","+","+See the xref:security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication.adoc#demonstrating-proof-of-possession-dpop[Demonstrating Proof of Possession for access tokens] section of the xref:security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication.adoc[OpenID Connect Bearer token authentication] guide for more information."," "," [[bearer-token-source-properties]]"," === Bearer token header","@@ -986,7 +1007,7 @@ In some cases, both the header and the scheme may have to customized."," `quarkus.oidc.token.header` and `quarkus.oidc.token.authorization-scheme` can be used to customize which HTTP header contains a bearer access token. You can customize the header and, when the HTTP `Authorization` is used - the scheme."," "," For example, you can set `quarkus.oidc.token.authorization-scheme=DPoP` to accept the DPoP access tokens sent as `Authorization: DPoP <token>`.","-See the xref:security-oidc-bearer-token-authentication#demonstrating-proof-of-possession-dpop[Demonstrating Proof of Possession] sectio